From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nix-on-droid <nix-on-droid@local>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] path: handle empty referrer in detranslate

Ports proot-me/proot 413abd6: readlinkat(2) with AT_EMPTY_PATH passes
an empty referrer path.  Returning early keeps the sanity_check and
follow_binding locals initialized (they are set in the symlink branch
below; falling through with an empty referrer would leave them
indeterminate).  Also drops the two `assert(length > 0)` in
compare_paths2(): they contradict the length check immediately below
them, where zero lengths legally return PATHS_ARE_NOT_COMPARABLE.

---
 src/path/path.c |    9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/path/path.c b/src/path/path.c
index d5c9ec6..4d088c3 100644
--- a/src/path/path.c
+++ b/src/path/path.c
@@ -416,6 +416,13 @@ int detranslate_path(Tracee *tracee, char path[PATH_MAX], const char t_referrer[
 	if (path[0] != '/')
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Don't try to detranslate when the referrer path is empty, e.g.
+	 * readlinkat(2) with AT_EMPTY_PATH (Linux >= 2.6.39).
+	 */
+	if (t_referrer != NULL && t_referrer[0] == '\0')
+		return 0;
+
 	/* Is it a symlink?  */
 	if (t_referrer != NULL) {
 		Comparison comparison;
@@ -543,8 +550,6 @@ Comparison compare_paths2(const char *path1, size_t length1, const char *path2,
 	assert(length(path1) == length1);
 	assert(length(path2) == length2);
 #endif
-	assert(length1 > 0);
-	assert(length2 > 0);
 
 	if (!length1 || !length2) {
 		return PATHS_ARE_NOT_COMPARABLE;
--
2.53.0
